-- cmd: check
-- exit: 1
-- The package check also checks each .silt file under tests/ that is no
-- test, as a program of its own whose imports are the package's
-- modules, as it does for a file in a sub-directory of src/: such a
-- file is no module (an import looks only in src/), and its error is
-- not passed over. A script there that imports a module checks clean.
import shapes

fn main() {
  println(shapes.two())
}
